 ],
 "note": "Appendix §H, Recovery, Astation's r4 trace. c1 executes P1 with P2 queued under control_gen 1. It loses control and the fence write fails with a successful rollback: no durable fence, the journal halts. After the restart (no clean close: the journal was halted) the principal is welcomed with control again at once, so the stored control_gen still equals P2's and a control flag can't show the missed revocation; P2 was nevertheless rejected (authorization history unknown) at startup, before c1 authenticated, and never runs, even 60 s later; the resend with the same id returns that receipt. Second cycle: P3 executes and P4 is queued (an acquiring Send by the holder), then the fence write and its rollback both fail, so the fence record may be on disk. The outcome is the same whatever reached the disk: P4 rejected (authorization history unknown), never dispatched; P1 and P3 outcome_unknown."
